{
  "tema": 6183,
  "slug": "preterito-progresivo",
  "titulo": "Forming the preterite progressive with estar + gerund",
  "subtitulo": "Estuve surfeando toda la tarde: an action that went on for a closed stretch of time.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "Estar in the preterite (estuve, estuviste, estuvo, estuvimos, estuvieron) + gerund (-ando, -iendo): estuve trabajando.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Every Spanish past tense has a progressive form for actions that were **ongoing** in the past. The **preterite progressive** is very close to the English past continuous: **estuve caminando**, _I was walking_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**estar** in the preterite",
            "gerund"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "estar (preterite)"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "estuve"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "estuviste"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "estuvo"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "estuvimos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "estuvieron"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Verb type",
            "Gerund",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "-ar",
              "-ando",
              "llamar → llamando"
            ],
            [
              "-er",
              "-iendo",
              "aprender → aprendiendo"
            ],
            [
              "-ir",
              "-iendo",
              "vivir → viviendo"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "This works for most regular verbs. Some verbs have irregular gerunds (**durmiendo**, **leyendo**, **corrigiendo**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It often comes with a time frame that has a clear start and end: **durante cuatro horas**, **hasta las diez**, **toda la noche**, **toda la tarde**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the preterite closes the box; the gerund fills it with action. A finished stretch of something happening."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Yo ==estuve caminando== durante cuatro horas.",
              "en": "I was walking for four hours."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tú ==estuviste corrigiendo== exámenes hasta las diez.",
              "en": "You were grading exams until ten."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ella ==estuvo bailando== con ese chavo toda la noche.",
              "en": "She was dancing with that guy all night."
            },
            {
              "es": "Nosotros ==estuvimos hablando== con los periodistas.",
              "en": "We were talking to the reporters."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ellos ==estuvieron arreglando== la llave del agua.",
              "en": "They were fixing the faucet."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ayer ==estuvimos surfeando== toda la tarde.",
              "en": "Yesterday we were surfing all afternoon."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
